prompt read the road ahead (REMEMBER · 1024-round itinerary · six-season double-seat · rye-first crypto decision wave); take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Rye prioritized; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates
think The living edge is Season G (Cryptography) with its serialization sibling encoding/. base64.rye landed as the only encoding rung; the encoding README named three next rungs — base58, base32, hex.
think Lindy-first crux-first among the three: base58 is the encoding Grain's own identity keys, content addresses, and the .sol/.sui reserve all wear (Kumara, Solana). It is also the hardest-solvable — arbitrary-length base conversion, and Zig ships no std base58 so there is no std cross-check the way base64 enjoys. Highest durable payoff, hardest tractable move — the crux.
think Mirrored base64.rye's shape exactly: opening triad, bounded max_decoded_bytes / max_encoded_bytes, named Base58Error, contract asserts (>=2/fn) each with a positive // invariant, edge refusals before any partial write.
think Solved the missing-std-parity honestly: authored a SECOND, independent encoder over Zig's native u128 integer inside the selftest (for payloads <=15 bytes = 120 bits), so parity is a genuine cross-implementation check, not a self-check. Anchored the real-world shapes on the canonical Bitcoin Core encode/decode known-answers, including the leading-zero and all-zero cases, plus a round-trip at every length.
think Primary algorithm is byte-array long division (base-256 folded into base-58 and back); the u128 reference is a different arithmetic path — agreement across both plus the published vectors is real evidence, not memory.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass: all twelve Bitcoin Core vectors matched text-for-text and round-tripped, u128 parity matched 0..15 bytes, BadChar / DestTooSmall refused at the edge. tame_style_check bans clean; base58.rye carries asserts (not on the zero-assert ratchet list).
obs Kept the rung atomic per the finishing edge — one file, one witness, README seated. base58check (payload + double-SHA-256 checksum) is now buildable on the GREEN crypto/sha256.rye and is named as the natural next composition, not started this round.
obs No custody gate touched — purely local arithmetic, no key, no network, no funds, no device.
